@description ambiX (.ambix) file support for REAPER, plus loudness-normalize and track-channel-count actions
@version 0.3.0
@author Matthias Kronlachner
@metapackage
@provides
  [darwin]          reaper_ambix.dylib https://github.com/kronihias/reaper_ambix/releases/download/v$version/reaper_ambix.dylib
  [win64]           reaper_ambix.dll   https://github.com/kronihias/reaper_ambix/releases/download/v$version/reaper_ambix-win64.dll
  [windows-arm64ec] reaper_ambix.dll   https://github.com/kronihias/reaper_ambix/releases/download/v$version/reaper_ambix-winarm64.dll
  [linux64]         reaper_ambix.so    https://github.com/kronihias/reaper_ambix/releases/download/v$version/reaper_ambix-x86_64.so
  [linux-aarch64]   reaper_ambix.so    https://github.com/kronihias/reaper_ambix/releases/download/v$version/reaper_ambix-aarch64.so
@link https://github.com/kronihias/reaper_ambix
@about
  # reaper_ambix

  REAPER extension adding read and write support for `.ambix` files following
  the ambiX (Ambisonics eXchangeable) specification. Output can be written
  uncompressed (CAF container) or with WavPack lossless compression; reading
  auto-detects the container.

  It also adds two actions to the main action list:

  **ambiX: Normalize selected item(s) to target loudness (LUFS)...**

  Measures the integrated loudness of each selected item to ITU-R BS.1770 and
  sets the take volume so it lands on the target you enter. Ambisonic items are
  measured on the W channel alone; surround beds use the BS.1770-5 Annex 3
  channel weighting up to 9.1.4.

  **ambiX: Set channel count of selected track(s) and their sends...**

  Sets the track channel count on every selected track and resizes the sends
  that carried those tracks' full width, so a whole encoder-into-bus chain
  changes ambisonic order in one step. Partial routings (mono sends, offset
  taps, hardware outputs) are left alone.

  Restart REAPER after installing or updating.
@changelog
  - New action: set the channel count of the selected tracks and resize the
    sends that carried their full width, for changing ambisonic order across a
    whole encoder-into-bus chain in one step. Native port of
    change_channel_count.py from the ambix plug-in suite - no Python needed
